OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774989770
OL,1,V7w3s7s35                          G4/17
OL,2,V55555555C47 POLICE HURT
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CIN POLL TAX PROTEST
OL,4,T
OL,5, Forty-seven police were injured and
OL,6, more than 100 people arrested as
OL,7, violence erupted after a huge anti-poll
OL,8, tax rally in Central London.
OL,10, Rioters torched and overturned cars,
OL,11, smashed windows and looted shops over a
OL,12, wide area during the rampage.
OL,14, Bottles, sticks and broken flag poles
OL,15, were hurled at officers as they tried
OL,16, to move demonstrators from Trafalgar
OL,17, Square along Whitehall.
OL,19, Many restaurants and pubs closed for
OL,20, the night as riot squads went into the
OL,21, Covent Garden area trying to quell
OL,22, sporadic outbreaks of violence.
OL,23,F]DFrom 31-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49605
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774989770
OL,1,V7w3s7s35B                         G5/17
OL,2,V55555555CPEACEFUL RALLY
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CTURNS TO VIOLENCE
OL,4,T
OL,5, Extremists have been blamed for trouble
OL,6, which erupted at a massive rally
OL,7, against the poll tax in Central London.
OL,9, Labour MP George Galloway said members
OL,10, of the Socialist Workers' Party stirred
OL,11, up trouble but the group denied claims
OL,12, and blamed a police "riot".
OL,14, MPs from both sides of Parliament hit
OL,15, out at the violence and blamed
OL,16, "mindless hooligans" and "professional
OL,17, militants."
OL,19, Tory MP David Wilshire said: "This is a
OL,20, sad day for democracy. The rule of
OL,21, Parliament and the rule of law no
OL,22, longer matters to some people."
OL,23,F]DFrom 31-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49606
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774989770
OL,1,V7w3s7s35T                         G6/17
OL,2,V55555555C200 IN CHELTENHAM
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CPOLL TAX RAMPAGE
OL,4,T
OL,5, Two police officers were hurt and 48
OL,6, people arrested when poll tax
OL,7, protesters went on the rampage outside
OL,8, the Tory conference in Cheltenham.
OL,10, Trouble broke out as Mrs Thatcher left
OL,11, the conference hall following a
OL,12, rallying call to the Party.
OL,14, A group of about 200 people had left a
OL,15, rally in a local park and converged on
OL,16, the town hall where they pelted police
OL,17, with stones and cans.
OL,19, A police spokesman said the official
OL,20, poll tax march had gone off peacefully
OL,21, and he suspected the organisers had no
OL,22, idea what was in store.
OL,23,F]DFrom 31-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49607
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774989770
OL,1,V7w3s7s35                          G7/17
OL,2,V55555555CI AM NOT RETIRING
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5C- DEFIANT THATCHER
OL,5, Mrs Thatcher has responded to questions
OL,6, about her future by telling the Tory
OL,7, Party faithful gathered at Cheltenham
OL,8, that she had not gone there to retire.
OL,10, She told the Conservative Central
OL,11, Council there might be 650 applicants -
OL,12, the number of MPs in the Commons - but
OL,13, there was no vacancy in Downing Street.
OL,15, Criticism was one of the "perks" of the
OL,16, job but she urged the Party to have the
OL,17, spirit and sheer guts to "grasp the
OL,18, shining future within our reach".
OL,20, She added: "I have the stomach for that
OL,21, fight and so, I believe, does Britain."
OL,23,F]DFrom 31-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
