OL,1,V7w3s7s35                          G8/17
OL,2,V55555555C GORBACHEV WARNS OF
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5C'GRAVE CONSEQUENCES'
OL,5, President Gorbachev warned Lithuania
OL,6, that failure to heed calls to abandon
OL,7, its self-proclaimed independence could
OL,8, lead to "grave consquences for us all".
OL,10, In his most ominous warning to date he
OL,11, added that "this path is ruinous and
OL,12, can only lead to a dead end".
OL,14, The rebel moves threatened the Baltic
OL,15, republic's security and he urged them
OL,16, to negotiate "within the framework of
OL,17, the USSR constitution."
OL,19,SGSoviet security forces earlier took
OL,20, over Lithuania's main newspaper
OL,21, publishing house.
OL,23,F]DFrom 31-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
